      <title>Meta &amp; Lyft Move Higher, Apple's Foldable iPhone | Stock Movers</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-09-09/meta-lyft-gain-apple-s-foldable-iphone-stock-movers-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">e0dee45e53fcc54e76d905a1</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 14:34:46 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>On this episode of Stock Movers:

- Meta (META) shares are gaining with analysts positive on the Facebook parent after it debuted Muse, an AI assistant. Firms wrote that Meta is well positioned to succeed with the product.

- Lyft (LYFT) shares are higher as the ride-hailing company is starting to offer Waymo robotaxi rides in Nashville, marking the second US city where it’s providing driverless trips.

- Apple (AAPL) shares are on the move ahead of today's product unveil. Apple's stock has rallied 15% since June 25, driven by excitement about the new lineup of devices, particularly the foldable phone. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
